==Latin==

===Etymology 1===
* From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*kezdō}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*ḱyesdʰ-||to drive away; to go away}}. Cognates include {{cog|sa|सेधति||to drive, chase away}} and {{cog|ae|𐬯𐬍𐬀𐬰𐬛𐬀𐬝||will chase away}}, from {{cog|iir-pro|*ćiazd-}}, {{m|iir-pro|*ćižd-}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|pages=103-104|head=cēdō, -ere}}</ref>
* Others refer to {{inh|la|itc-pro|*kezdō}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*ḱye}}, adverb from {{m|ine-pro|*ḱe||here}}, + {{m|ine-pro|*sed-||to sit}}. Compare with the semantics of English [[set]] [[out]] and Ancient Greek {{m|grc|ὁδός}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|eccl=1|vul=yes|cēdō}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|3|cēdō|cess|cess}}

# {{lb|la|intransitive}} I [[go]], [[move]], [[proceed]], [[go along]], [[move]] along.
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Pseudolus|4|1|44|thru=45|quote=SIMŌ. Illīcine est? PSEUDOLUS. Illīc est. SIMŌ. Mala merx est, Pseudole. Illūc sīs vidē,<br>ut trānsvorsus, nōn prōvorsus '''cēdit''', quasi cancer solet.|trans=SIMO. Is he there? PSEUDOLUS. There he is. SIMO. He's a bad piece, Pseudolus. Look at that,<br>how he '''goes''' sideways, not forwards, as a crab does.}}
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} I [[result]], [[turn out]], [[happen]].
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} I [[withdraw]], [[depart]], [[retire]], go away from.
## {{lb|la|intransitive|military}} I withdraw, [[fall back]], [[give up]] my post.
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} I [[disappear]], [[pass away]], [[vanish]].
# {{lb|la|intransitive|with dative}} I [[cede]], [[give in]] or [[yield]] (to), [[step aside]] (for), [[give way]] (to).
#* [[w:Virgil|Vergilius]], [[w:Aeneid|Aeneis]], Book VI, line 95
#*: Tū nē '''cēde''' malīs, sed contrā audentior ītō
#*:: '''Give in''' not to evils, but go against them more daring.
#* Motto of Wyoming
#*: '''Cēdant''' arma togae.
#*:: Let the arms '''concede''' to the toga (Let war yield to diplomacy)
## {{lb|la|intransitive}} I am [[inferior]] to, yield to in rank.
# {{lb|la|transitive}} I [[concede]], give up, [[grant]], [[surrender]], [[yield]].
# {{lb|la|intransitive|with dative or in +acc.}} I [[fall]] (to) (as a possession); [[accrue]] or [[come]] (to).
# {{lb|la|intransitive|with in +acc.}} I [[become]], [[turn into]], be or become the [[equivalent]] of.

